cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the data it produces, please cite it as below."
title: "bd-boro-data-framework: an open, tested data engineering framework for integrating official crop statistics with satellite and climate data, district-level Boro rice in Bangladesh"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mumu
    given-names: Tasnim Ahmad
    affiliation: "Department of Agronomy and Agricultural Extension, University of Rajshahi"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-8346-9622"
version: "1.0.0-dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TasMumu/bd-boro-data-framework"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Bronze–Silver–Gold pipeline in Python and DuckDB that extracts district
  Boro rice statistics from the Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics Yearbooks of
  Agricultural Statistics (2012–2025 editions), validates every value against
  unit identities, printed national totals and a second edition, and aligns
  it by harvest year with MODIS NDVI, ERA5-Land climate, and JRC and
  Sentinel-1 flood fractions for all 64 districts (harvest years 2011–2025).
  The pipeline code and documentation are in the folder v2.
keywords:
  - data engineering
  - reproducibility
  - agricultural statistics
  - Boro rice
  - Bangladesh
  - Sentinel-1
  - DuckDB
